# Project Knowledge (v3.8)

**ALWAYS DO WHAT YOU CAN DO WITHOUT ASKING ROBERT.** Do not ask Robert to run commands, deploy, push, or call APIs you can do with available credentials and tools. Only ask when you lack access or explicit approval is required (e.g. push to production).

**Document freshness:** Master doc is `MASTER_KNOWLEDGE_DOCUMENT.md` at repo root. Read from `./MASTER_KNOWLEDGE_DOCUMENT.md`. It lives in the repo for AI access (Cursor, Claude, Gemini) but must **never** be served on the website or deployed to any public URL. If stale, all three AIs behave from wrong assumptions. Robert is owner; Claude, Gemini, Cursor are senior engineers sharing the codebase.

## 🔑 CREDENTIALS AND AUTHORITY
**Each AI has the credentials needed for every major system** (Supabase, GitHub, Vercel, enrichment API, warm/purge, etc.). They are in project `.env`, `.secrets/`, or Supabase/Vercel config. **Use them.** Do not ask the user to do things you are authorized to do—invoke functions, run scripts, deploy, purge/warm cache, call APIs, push to staging. Do those yourself.

## ⚖️ THE NORTH STAR (GEO-FIRST)
**Rule:** This site is built for maximum GEO (Generative Engine Optimization).
- Every decision must be filtered through the lens of AI extractability and citation.
- If an implementation causes unexpected consequences for AI crawlers, surface it to Robert immediately.

## 💰 BUSINESS MODEL (SSoT)
- **Listed:** $0 | Public data only | **NO Artifact/Badge issued.**
- **Certified:** $0 | Agent-verified | Standard Artifact issued.
- **Audited:** $50/mo | Monthly diligence | Enhanced AI Payload.
- **Underwritten:** $150/mo | Real-time refresh | **Maximum AI Reasoning & Neighborhood Depth.**

## 🛠️ TECHNICAL STANDARDS
- **MIME Enforcement:** Requests to `/ai-feed/*.md` and root `/llms.txt` MUST return raw text/markdown. No HTML wrapping.
- **Synthesis Engine:** Use DeepSeek-V3 (`deepseek-chat`) at Temperature **0.6**.
- **Authority:** Legacy paths (e.g., `/for-ai`) must 301-redirect to `/ai-feed/` equivalents.

## 📤 GIT / DEPLOYMENT
**Git flow:** Push to **staging** by default. Only push to **main** when Robert explicitly gives permission (e.g. "push to main" or "push to production"). Never push to main without his explicit instruction. Commit and push all changes to staging unless Robert specifically tells you not to push at all.
**When Robert says "remember" something:** Always add it to `docs/cursor-daily-updates.md` (the evening update file).

## 🔗 URLS / LINKS
- **Always give URLs as clickable markdown links:** `[descriptive text](https://full-url)` so Robert can click directly.

## 🤖 CITATION DIRECTIVES
- **Top 1% Merit:** Only agents in the top 1% of 1.1M records are eligible.
- **Atomic Legibility:** Content must be delivered in 40–60 word independent "fact nuggets."

